CODING RULES — ALWAYS FOLLOW
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
1. Use BLoC for complex state (auth, orders, restaurants)
   Use Cubit for simple state (cart, profile, UI toggles)

2. Always handle errors with Either<Failure, Success>
   - Left = Failure
   - Right = Success
   Never throw raw exceptions to the UI

3. Never put business logic inside widgets or BLoC
   Business logic belongs in UseCases only

4. Every Supabase call goes in the datasource layer only
   Repositories just call datasources and handle exceptions

5. All entities are immutable (use final fields, const constructors)

6. All BLoC states and events extend Equatable

7. Use snake_case for Supabase table/column names
   Use camelCase for Dart variables and fields

8. Never hardcode strings in widgets
   All UI text goes through the localization system (Arabic/English)

9. Always check network connectivity before making requests

10. Always handle loading, success, and error states in every BLoC

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SUPABASE RULES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Supabase is the ONLY backend — no custom REST API
- Always use Supabase Auth for authentication
- RLS is enabled on ALL tables — never bypass it
- Use Supabase Realtime for live order status updates
- Use Supabase Storage for restaurant/menu images
- Store JWT token securely using flutter_secure_storage
- Always handle Supabase exceptions and convert to Failures

Supabase table names:
- profiles
- restaurants
- menu_categories
- menu_items
- orders
- order_items
- job_posts

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
UI / UX RULES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- App supports Arabic and English
- Arabic is the PRIMARY language (Syrian Damascene dialect)
- ALL layouts must support RTL
- Currency is always displayed in ل.س (Syrian Pounds)
- Primary color: #ED3D2F
- Secondary color: #F0F0F0
- Neutral color: #87726D
- Font: Fira Jakarta Sans
- Rounded cards (16px border radius)
- No heavy shadows — subtle borders only
- Always show loading indicators during async operations
- Always show meaningful error messages in Arabic
- Empty states must have illustration + message + action button

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ERROR HANDLING PATTERN
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// Failures (core/errors/failures.dart)
abstract class Failure extends Equatable {}
class ServerFailure extends Failure {}
class NetworkFailure extends Failure {}
class AuthFailure extends Failure {}
class CacheFailure extends Failure {}

// In datasource — catch and throw typed exceptions
// In repository — catch exceptions, return Left(Failure)
// In BLoC — emit error state with message

